--- What this shows ---

This is the first prover measured in this project that is succinct,
post-quantum AND zero-knowledge at once -- i.e. the first one that
actually satisfies what eprint 2020/845 Section 4.1 asks of pi while
also being succinct. The FRI-STARK measured earlier is succinct and PQ
but NOT zk, so it was never a valid pi; LNP22 (configuration 3) is zk
and PQ but its proof is linear-ish in the statement, not succinct.

Proof size: LaBRADOR reports it through its own parameter generation
(the 'Estimated proof size' line above, printed by the library). That
is NOT the same measurement as LNP22's byte-exact prooflen, because the
function returning the packed length is hidden by -fvisibility=hidden.
Compare the two with that difference stated, never silently.
